+## Cycle 5 — Root cause identified: editingId not cleared on destroy
 
-Two acceptance-suite failures remain after the DOM-identity fix.
-Both are real product defects visible only in a real browser.
+**Acceptance test:** `should remove the item if an empty text string was entered`
+**Spec:** `features/browser-acceptance-defects.feature:44` (new `@contract` scenario)
+**Root cause refined:** The `parentNode` guard in the orphan-removal loop (added in Cycle 3) prevents the crash in isolation, but `destroyTodo()` does NOT clear `editingId`. When both `blur` and `keydown(Enter)` fire during real-browser editing-to-empty, the sequence is:
+1. `blur` → `finishEditing()` → `destroyTodo()` → `render()` → orphan removed
+2. `keydown(Enter)` → `finishEditing()` → `destroyTodo()` → `render()` → orphan re-attached (because `editingId` still matches) then removed again
 
-### Defect BROWSER-1: removeChild during re-entrant blur (editing to empty)
+The re-attachment during the second `render()` is the defect. The `parentNode` guard catches it in the simple case, but the re-entrant blur timing in a real browser creates the `removeChild` error.
 
-**Acceptance test:** `should remove the item if an empty text string was entered`
-**Spec:** `features/browser-acceptance-defects.feature:27`
-**Root cause:** When the user clears the edit input and presses Enter, both `blur` and `keydown(Enter)` fire. Both call `finishEditing()` → `destroyTodo()` → `render()`. The first `render()` removes the `<li>` via `removeChild`, which detaches the `<input>`, firing `blur` synchronously mid-orphan-removal-loop. The blur handler re-enters `render()`, removing the same orphan. The original loop's `existingLis[j]` now references a node whose `parentNode` no longer considers it a child → `removeChild` throws `NotFoundError`.
-**Fix指引:**
-1. Guard the orphan-removal loop: only call `removeChild` if `existingLis[j].parentNode === todoList` (or simply check `parentNode` is not null)
-2. Clear `editingId` in `destroyTodo()` to prevent stale editing state
+**Fix指引:** Add `editingId = null;` in `destroyTodo()` when the destroyed todo is the one being edited.
+
+### Previous defects (resolved)
+
+- DOM-identity (toggle/destroy) — resolved by in-place DOM mutation in render()
+- parentNode guard — added but insufficient alone; the editingId-clear fix is the true fix
 
